IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa24-disclosure.l4: Part 35 "Disclosure of information", ss 1110E to 1110G of the Companies Act 2006 (lines 15941-15969
-- of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT ENCODED. s 1110F(2) (the affirmative resolution procedure for regulations) is machinery: inert (reason 2) in
-- NOTES.md. The Data Protection Act 2018, the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005 and the regulations under
-- s 1110F(1)(c) are not among the sources; whether a disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation, and what
-- the regulations say, come in as facts or inputs.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST TRUE is the text
-- saying yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`); NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why,
-- as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). s 1110G(6) is a defence: the ruling of 2026-11-05 (b) says the answer is JUST FALSE, worded
-- "this section gives no defence on these facts", when what the person must prove is not proved.

§ `Part 35: disclosure of information (ss 1110E to 1110G)`

-- ---- s 1110E ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15943 | Any person may disclose information to the registrar for the purposes of the exercise of any of the registrar’s functions.
@ref s 1110E Any person may disclose information to the registrar (src:15943)
GIVEN `the disclosure is for the purposes of the exercise of any of the registrar's functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110E the person may disclose the information to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is for the purposes of the exercise of any of the registrar's functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of the exercise of any of the registrar’s functions"

-- ---- s 1110F ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1110F(1) recipient and purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 1110F(1)(a) any person, for purposes connected with the exercise of any of the registrar's functions`
    `s 1110F(1)(b) a public authority, for purposes connected with the exercise of any of that public authority's functions`
    `s 1110F(1)(c) a person of a description, and for a purpose, specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State`
    `s 1110F(1) another recipient or purpose`

-- src:15945 | (1) The registrar may disclose information—
-- src:15946 | (a) to any person for purposes connected with the exercise of any of the registrar’s functions;
-- src:15947 | (b) to a public authority for purposes connected with the exercise of any of that public authority’s functions;
-- src:15948 | (c) to a person of a description, and for a purpose, specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 1110F(1) Disclosure by the registrar (src:15945-15948)
GIVEN recipient IS A `s 1110F(1) recipient and purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110F(1) the registrar may disclose the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `s 1110F(1)(a) any person, for purposes connected with the exercise of any of the registrar's functions` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1110F(1)(b) a public authority, for purposes connected with the exercise of any of that public authority's functions` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1110F(1)(c) a person of a description, and for a purpose, specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1110F(1) another recipient or purpose` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists the cases in which the registrar may disclose and does not close the list with "only"

-- src:15950 | (3) In this section “public authority” includes any person or body having functions of a public nature.
@ref s 1110F(3) "public authority" (src:15950)
GIVEN `the person or body has functions of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110F(3) the person or body is a public authority` MEANS
    IF `the person or body has functions of a public nature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“public authority” includes any person or body having functions of a public nature"

-- ---- s 1110G ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15952 | (1) Except as provided by subsection (2), the disclosure of information under section 1110E or 1110F does not breach—
-- src:15953 | (a) any obligation of confidence owed by the person making the disclosure, or
-- src:15954 | (b) any other restriction on the disclosure of information (however imposed).
-- src:15955 | (2) Sections 1110E and 1110F do not authorise a disclosure of information if the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation (but in determining whether a disclosure would do so, take into account the powers conferred by those sections).
@ref s 1110G(1)-(2) The effect of disclosure under ss 1110E and 1110F, and its limit (src:15952-15955)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under section 1110E or 1110F` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation (taking into account the powers conferred by sections 1110E and 1110F)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110G(1) the disclosure breaches an obligation of confidence or any other restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure was made under section 1110E or 1110F` AND (NOT `the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation (taking into account the powers conferred by sections 1110E and 1110F)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the disclosure of information under section 1110E or 1110F does not breach— (a) any obligation of confidence owed by the person making the disclosure, or (b) any other restriction on the disclosure of information (however imposed)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as provided by subsection (2)" the protection covers a disclosure under section 1110E or 1110F, and subsection (2) takes a disclosure that would contravene the data protection legislation out of it

@ref s 1110G(2) Sections 1110E and 1110F do not authorise a disclosure that would contravene the data protection legislation (src:15955)
GIVEN `the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation (taking into account the powers conferred by sections 1110E and 1110F)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110G(2) sections 1110E and 1110F authorise the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation (taking into account the powers conferred by sections 1110E and 1110F)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sections 1110E and 1110F do not authorise a disclosure of information if the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says when the sections do not authorise and does not say when they do

-- src:15956 | (3) HMRC information may not be disclosed by the registrar under section 1110F without authorisation from HMRC.
-- src:15957 | (4) If the registrar discloses HMRC information under section 1110F, the information must not be disclosed by the recipient, or by any person obtaining the information directly or indirectly from them, without authorisation from HMRC.
@ref s 1110G(3)-(4) HMRC information (src:15956-15957)
GIVEN `the information is HMRC information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorisation from HMRC has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110G(3) the registrar may disclose the information under section 1110F` MEANS
    IF `the information is HMRC information` AND (NOT `authorisation from HMRC has been given`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "HMRC information may not be disclosed by the registrar under section 1110F without authorisation from HMRC"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars disclosure of HMRC information without authorisation; it does not itself grant the power, which is in section 1110F

@ref s 1110G(4) The recipient must not disclose the information without authorisation from HMRC (src:15957)
GIVEN `the registrar disclosed HMRC information under section 1110F` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorisation from HMRC has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110G(4) the recipient, or a person obtaining the information from the recipient, may disclose the information` MEANS
    IF `the registrar disclosed HMRC information under section 1110F` AND (NOT `authorisation from HMRC has been given`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the information must not be disclosed by the recipient, or by any person obtaining the information directly or indirectly from them, without authorisation from HMRC"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars disclosure without authorisation; it does not itself grant a power to disclose

-- src:15958 | (5) It is an offence for a person to disclose, in contravention of subsection (3) or (4), any revenue and customs information relating to a person whose identity—
-- src:15959 | (a) is specified in the disclosure, or
-- src:15960 | (b) can be deduced from it.
@ref s 1110G(5) The offence of disclosing revenue and customs information in contravention of subsection (3) or (4) (src:15958-15960)
GIVEN `the person disclosed revenue and customs information in contravention of subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to a person whose identity is specified in the disclosure or can be deduced from it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110G(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person disclosed revenue and customs information in contravention of subsection (3) or (4)` AND `the information relates to a person whose identity is specified in the disclosure or can be deduced from it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person to disclose, in contravention of subsection (3) or (4), any revenue and customs information relating to a person whose identity— (a) is specified in the disclosure, or (b) can be deduced from it"

-- src:15961 | (6) It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under subsection (5) to prove that the person reasonably believed—
-- src:15962 | (a) that the disclosure was lawful, or
-- src:15963 | (b) that the information had already lawfully been made available to the public.
@ref s 1110G(6) A defence for a person charged under subsection (5) who proves a reasonable belief (src:15961-15963)
GIVEN `the person proves that they reasonably believed that the disclosure was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that they reasonably believed that the information had already lawfully been made available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110G(6) this section gives a defence` MEANS
    IF `the person proves that they reasonably believed that the disclosure was lawful` OR `the person proves that they reasonably believed that the information had already lawfully been made available to the public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under subsection (5) to prove that the person reasonably believed— (a) that the disclosure was lawful, or (b) that the information had already lawfully been made available to the public" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:15964 | (7) Subsections (4) to (7) of section 19 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005 apply to an offence under subsection (5) as they apply to an offence under that section.
@ref s 1110G(7) Section 19(4) to (7) of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005 apply to the offence (src:15964)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110G(7) subsections (4) to (7) of section 19 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005 apply to the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is an offence under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to an offence under subsection (5)"

-- src:15965 | (8) In this section—
-- src:15966 | “the data protection legislation” has the same meaning as in the Data Protection Act 2018 (see section 3 of that Act);
-- src:15967 | “HMRC” means the Commissioners for His Majesty’s Revenue and Customs;
-- src:15968 | “HMRC information” means information disclosed to the registrar under section 1110E by HMRC or a person acting on behalf of HMRC;
-- src:15969 | “revenue and customs information relating to a person” has the meaning given by section 19(2) of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005.
@ref s 1110G(8) The defined terms (src:15965-15969)
GIVEN `the information was disclosed to the registrar under section 1110E` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was disclosed by HMRC or a person acting on behalf of HMRC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110G(8) the information is HMRC information` MEANS
    IF `the information was disclosed to the registrar under section 1110E` AND `the information was disclosed by HMRC or a person acting on behalf of HMRC`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“HMRC information” means information disclosed to the registrar under section 1110E by HMRC or a person acting on behalf of HMRC"

@ref s 1110G(8) "HMRC" (src:15967)
GIVEN `the body is the Commissioners for His Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1110G(8) the body is HMRC` MEANS
    IF `the body is the Commissioners for His Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“HMRC” means the Commissioners for His Majesty’s Revenue and Customs"

@ref s 1110G(8) "the data protection legislation" (src:15966)
`s 1110G(8) the provision that gives the meaning of "the data protection legislation"` MEANS "section 3 of the Data Protection Act 2018"

@ref s 1110G(8) "revenue and customs information relating to a person" (src:15969)
`s 1110G(8) the provision that gives the meaning of "revenue and customs information relating to a person"` MEANS "section 19(2) of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005"
